ite. Read more Mentoring and Advising Explore college-specific mentoring and advising resources. Read more Michael Sweet, Healthy Body, Healthy Mind: Mindfulness and Meditation For information on this topic, please go to the “Faculty Affairs” tab of this website. Read more Michele Grazulis, Vice President & Chief Human Resources Officer and Diane Levin, University Ombuds, University Resources and Available Assistance For information on this topic, please go to the “Faculty Affairs” tab of this website. Read more New Degree Program Proposal Guidelines Detailed steps of Planning and Approving of New Degree Programs. Read more New Degree Proposal Routing Form Northeastern University’s online form for proposing new degrees. Read more New Graduate Certificate (Non-CAGS) Proposal Guidelines Northeastern University’s Office of the Provost oversees the planning and approval of new Graduate Certificate programs. The process involves specific steps, with emphasis on joint preparation for requests in cross-college collaborative programs. Read more Northeastern University Health and Counseling Services Northeastern University Health and Counseling Services aims to enhance student well-being through research, education, and advocacy. Read more Northeastern Writing Center Open to students, faculty, and staff, gain writing help at any level. Read more NUpath Northeastern’s academic core integrates broad-based knowledge and skills for diverse disciplines. Read more NUPD Advisory Board To guide, inform, and strengthen NUPD’s relationship with the community—both within and outside Northeastern. Read more Office of Diversity, Equity and Inclusion The office develops the fluency necessary to reject discrimination, learn in a diverse, global society. Read more Ombuds for Faculty and Staff Safe space for faculty and staff to discuss workplace concerns, ensuring fair and equitable treatment. Read more Ombuds for Graduate Students The Ombuds for Graduate Students offers confidential, impar